# Detector benchmark

How often each metric fires on reference datasets, and how often it catches a defect injected into them.

- The datasets are *believed* clean. Nobody has verified that.
- A metric's benign rate is the share of the episodes it graded that it graded warning or critical.
- A detection cell reads `detected/eligible`. It counts only injections where the metric graded good at that spot before injection.
- Value defects are scaled to the channel they are injected into: {% for key, value in benchmark.injection.items() %}{{ key }} {{ "%g"|format(value) }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.
- A blank detection cell means the metric was not graded there. The LeRobot sets' reconstructed clocks leave every timing cell blank.
- Regenerate this file with `uv run kalanos benchmark --out docs/BENCHMARK.md`.

